<binaryimage arch="MIPS:BE:32:default:default">
<!--
    kuna option bejoin callers (the default), GH-904: MIPS PIC callers and
    unaligned loads.

    MIPS PIC code (gcc's and clang's default for a shared object) calls
    through the GOT, `lw $25,%call16(add64)($28); jalr $25`, so the caller
    evidence, which scanned only for jal/bal, saw no caller of add64 and its
    64-bit sum stayed joined low word first:
        return CONCAT44(a1 + a3,(uint4)(a1 + a3 < a1) + a0 + a2);   (bug)
    A jalr $25 is now a call to the function the GOT entry its load names
    holds, read at the GOT pointer the caller's prologue computes from $t9,
    when nothing between the load and the call branches or writes the
    registers it uses.  c_add stores both words of add64's pair.

    An unaligned load into $3 right after a call (lwl $3,1($16);
    lwr $3,4($16)) named $3 as an input, since each half merges memory into
    the register, and read as the call's low word: add_hi, the int over the
    high word of a sum, which leaves the carry in $3, was proven 64-bit by
    c_unal and c_unal joined its call v0:v1.  The pair overwrites $3 and
    reads nothing of it.

    Stage: P4 calls and prototypes (output-prototype), option bejoin.
    Pass 1 is the default (callers), pass 2 option bejoin evidence.

    Images: decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/bejoin_mipspic_O2.so
    (bejoin_mipspic.c) and bejoin_mipsunal (bejoin_mipsunal.S); see
    bejoin_mipspic.provenance.

    Assert #1: the default returns add64's sum high word first; evidence
      keeps it low word first, and add_hi stays an int in both passes.
    Assert #2: c_unal joins add_hi's result $3 high (the default join) in
      both passes, since nothing of $3 is read after the call.  It runs with
      option mipsunaligned off, which lifts the pair as two merges reading
      $3; on, the pair is one load and reads nothing of $3
      (kuna-mipsunaligned.xml).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">03e0000800000000</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
